CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F418A1786124905
OL,3,CMichelle O'Neill accuses DUP of being
OL,4,C'anti-Irish'
OL,6,FMichelle O'Neill said: "We know that
OL,7,Fwe have one partner around that
OL,8,FExecutive table that is anti-Irish in
OL,9,Ftheir approach, thathas an approach
OL,10,Fwhich is about delay and frustrating
OL,11,Fprogress.
OL,13,F"However, I will continue to turn up
OL,14,Fevery day because I believe in making
OL,15,Fpowersharing work. I believe in trying
OL,16,Fto do our very best for people. I
OL,17,Fbelieve in fighting for a fair budget
OL,18,Ffor people," she added.
OL,1,W~k4 jw=hw1 hw}h7}j7}            G2/7
OL,2,W/*% /*%/"-$+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNI NewsCClean Feed FThis Day
FL,419,410,140,120,000,100
PN,41803
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F418A1786124905
OL,3,CMichelle O'Neill accuses DUP of being
OL,4,C'anti-Irish'
OL,6,F"I think what's been articulated by
OL,7,Fboth Conor (Murphy) and also my
OL,8,Fcolleague Declan Kearney is the
OL,9,Ffrustration that people feel because
OL,10,Fof the DUP's approach to the
OL,11,FExecutive."
OL,13,FEmma Little-Pengelly said: "I think
OL,14,Fthere's a real sense of manufactured
OL,15,Foutrage. I think that there's a real
OL,16,Fsense that Sinn Fein at the moment are
OL,17,Ftrying to ramp things up.
OL,26,@xD@Rrr
OL,1,W~k4 jw=hw1 hw}h7}j7}            G3/7
OL,2,W/*% /*%/"-$+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNI NewsCClean Feed FThis Day
FL,419,410,140,120,000,100
PN,41804
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F418A1786124905
OL,3,CMichelle O'Neill accuses DUP of being
OL,4,C'anti-Irish'
OL,6,F"I don't know why but, of course, for
OL,7,Fmy part and for the part of my party
OL,8,Fand my DUP colleagues in the
OL,9,FExecutive, we will continue to get on
OL,10,Fand do the work."
OL,12,FIn Belfast, Micheal Martin was asked
OL,13,Fhow concerned he was about the
OL,14,Fstability of Stormont.
OL,16,FHe responded: "I think there is an
OL,17,Fobligation on all political parties to
OL,18,Fensure that Stormont is maintained,
OL,19,Fthe Executive and the Assembly right
OL,20,Fup to election day.
OL,26,@tD@RrpxD@OOU
OL,1,W~k4 jw=hw1 hw}h7}j7}            G4/7
OL,2,W/*% /*%/"-$+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
